E AX3040 353-callback-tyvar.ax:50:5-11 result-only-tyvar "`demand` must produce a value of type variable `a`, which no parameter supplies: it occurs inside a function-typed parameter, on the side this function fills in, so the caller chooses the type and an `as` conversion fabricates the value" ?"making the function diverge does not answer this one - the value is fabricated before it returns, or fails to; name a concrete word type in the callback's parameter and let callers write `as`, or tag the declaration `;@axiom:raw` to put it in the unsafe layer on purpose"
E AX3040 353-callback-tyvar.ax:64:5-15 result-only-tyvar "`alsoResult` returns type variable `a`, which no parameter mentions, and its body produces that result rather than never returning: the caller chooses the type and an `as` conversion fabricates the value" ?"three ways out: return a concrete word type and let callers write `as`; or make it DIVERGE, so every path ends in a call that never returns, which is what makes `for all a` honest; or tag the declaration `;@axiom:raw` to put it in the unsafe layer on purpose"
E AX3040 353-callback-tyvar.ax:68:5-14 result-only-tyvar "`divDemand` must produce a value of type variable `a`, which no parameter supplies: it occurs inside a function-typed parameter, on the side this function fills in, so the caller chooses the type and an `as` conversion fabricates the value" ?"making the function diverge does not answer this one - the value is fabricated before it returns, or fails to; name a concrete word type in the callback's parameter and let callers write `as`, or tag the declaration `;@axiom:raw` to put it in the unsafe layer on purpose"
E AX3073 353-callback-tyvar.ax:52:7-9 undeclared-unsafe "`demand` forges `a` out of `Int` with `as`, and its declaration does not say so" #"forges a reference" ^52:10-12:"source has type `Int`; the conversion trusts its representation" ?51:1:"write `;@axiom:effect(unsafe)` above the declaration"~>";@axiom:effect(unsafe)\n" ?"prefer a constructor or a typed library operation. For a raw conversion, prove the target's layout and validity, and keep its backing owner alive. Changing the type does not extend a region's scope" ?"the unsafe tag marks a trusted boundary: you must make every well-typed call safe. It leaves ordinary type, effect and restriction checks in place"
